oth removed himself from the ballot. All ten expert ratings call the race Safe or Solid Republican, and prediction markets give Risch roughly 93 to 95 percent.\n\nSurvey results have been strangely divergent, with some outlier polls even showing Achilles ahead, but the most recent readings put Risch up by around 25 points, and fundamentals point to a double-digit win. Achilles's consolidated anti-Risch coalition and a favorable national map give Democrats an outside story to watch, but outside money would need to arrive late and in volume to change the picture.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0267, "margin": -10.92}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0421, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0262, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0261, "margin": -13.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0155, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0312, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0381, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.01, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0098, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.1557, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0384, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0175, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0222, "margin": -15.0}]}